-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 73 DOWN: no-op.
--
-- Migration 73 is a data-only backfill: it rewrites `source.processing_stage`
-- VALUES for legacy rows that were at `"ingested"`, deriving the true stage from
-- each source's outputs. It defines no schema (the field itself is owned by
-- migration 71, whose own down removes it). A faithful inverse would have to
-- restore the pre-73 value ("ingested") for exactly the rows this migration
-- touched — but that information is not recorded, and blindly resetting derived
-- rows back to "ingested" would REINTRODUCE the very bug 73 fixes (and could
-- clobber rows the live pipeline advanced in the meantime). So the honest
-- rollback is to leave the derived, correct values in place.
-- ============================================================================

-- Intentionally empty (data-only forward migration; no schema to revert).
RETURN NONE;
